# The gates that judge a change, and the hooks that run them early (21/11/2026). `*` already
# covers them. In CODEOWNERS the LAST matching line wins, so these lines override
# the broader lines above them and nothing else: keep them last, and give any line added after them
# that matches these paths an owner, or it leaves them unowned. A change can edit the check that
# judges it in the same commit, so these always want a close read. main's ruleset does not require
# code-owner review, by decision (21/11/2026): the sole owner cannot approve their own pull
# request, so requiring it would send every merge through the admin bypass, which skips the
# required checks as well (and can force-push or delete main).
